# Original request of the change
```
#382 (d38da5e) set \`modeRequiresAllowance\` for every path whose new mode is 100755 and put it first in \`binaryPaths\`, so **any** edit to an executable text script (e.g. \`scripts/land-pr.sh\`) is reported as \`[binary-content] … binary bytes, such as a NUL\` and needs \`Allow: binary\`. #382's request and its test (\`executable image additions and mode-only changes need a binary allowance\`, all \`.png\`) are about executable *media* passing as inert. Run <run-id> (#376) spent three implementation rounds hunting NUL bytes that weren't there (verified: no NUL or control bytes; git's numstat treats the files as text).

Fix: the mode condition applies only to paths matching \`INERT_MEDIA_PATH\` (where it removes the inert-media exemption). Opaque binaries already need the allowance through the existing \`!inert\` branch; text files, executable or not, are diffed and reviewed like any other text.

Tests: new \`text scripts may be executable, edited, added or chmodded without a binary allowance\` (fails on main with 5 flagged paths, passes now); the existing executable-image test still passes; \`test/git-integrity.test.ts\` 188/188.

🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
```


