    "detail": "`textAt` sets `binary: bytes.includes(0) || bytes.includes(Buffer.from(\"%PDF-\"))`. This matches the five bytes anywhere in the blob, not only at the start of a PDF. Any source or test file that mentions the PDF magic number is removed from `raw` and ends up in `binaryPaths`. The user then sees the \"binary bytes, such as a NUL\" message even though there is no NUL. This change is an example: `src/git/repos.ts` (line 834) and `test/git-integrity.test.ts` (the `%PDF-1.4` fixtures) are both reported as binary by `diffSince` on c033a43..HEAD, with either the base or head code. That explains the factory audit flags on this review. The issue predates this diff and the request did not ask for it, but"
