    "detail": "textAt sets `binary: bytes.includes(0) || bytes.includes(Buffer.from(\"%PDF-\"))` for every blob, and binary paths are dropped from `raw`. So any edited text source that mentions \"%PDF-\" anywhere ends up in binaryPaths through the `!afterText.raw.has(path) && !inert.has(path)` branch. The audit then tells the author the file has \"binary bytes, such as a NUL\". This is why the automated audit flagged both files in this very change: both contain \"%PDF-\" and neither contains a NUL. It is the same wild-goose chase the request describes, from a different trigger. This predates the diff and is outside the request's scope."
